From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Date: Mon, 09 Nov 2026 11:25:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: HT-PHY: give the BCM4331 a block of four MAC addresses

The ucode matches all BSSIDs of a multi-AP setup with one base address
under a mask, so they must lie in one aligned block of four addresses.
The SPROM holds one address, and userspace takes the further APs'
addresses from wiphy->addresses or makes them up, mostly outside the
block, so a second SSID would only work with addresses set by hand.

On core rev 29, offer a block of four: the locally administered form of
the SPROM address (bit 1 of the first byte set, so the block never holds
the wired ports' global addresses) with the low two bits running 0-3,
in wiphy->addresses, and the first of them as the permanent address.
OpenWrt assigns them to the APs in order.

The first AP's address changes once from the SPROM address to its
locally administered form, also on single-AP setups.

Tested on the R6400 v2: with no address set in the configuration, the
two SSIDs came up as ce:..:38 and ce:..:39 and ran the 200-cycle soak.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h  |    2 +
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c |   27 +++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
@@ -1022,6 +1022,8 @@ struct b43_wl {
 	 * the microcode sends; these go out from the driver at its TBTT.
 	 */
 	struct ieee80211_vif *mbss_vif[B43_MBSS_MAX - 1];
+	/* The BSSID block offered to userspace where further APs can run */
+	struct mac_address mbss_addrs[B43_MBSS_MAX];
 	/* The MAC address of the operating interface. */
 	u8 mac_addr[ETH_ALEN];
 	/* Current BSSID */
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -7140,10 +7140,33 @@ static struct b43_wl *b43_wireless_init(
 	wl->hw_registered = false;
 	hw->max_rates = 2;
 	SET_IEEE80211_DEV(hw, dev->dev);
-	if (is_valid_ether_addr(sprom->et1mac))
+	if (dev->core_rev == B43_MBSS_CORE_REV) {
+		/*
+		 * All BSSIDs must lie in one aligned block (the ucode compares
+		 * one base address under a mask). Use the locally administered
+		 * form of the factory address, so the block never holds the
+		 * global addresses of the wired ports, and offer all of it to
+		 * userspace, which assigns them to the APs in order.
+		 */
+		const u8 *fac = is_valid_ether_addr(sprom->et1mac) ?
+				sprom->et1mac : sprom->il0mac;
+		unsigned int i;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < B43_MBSS_MAX; i++) {
+			u8 *a = wl->mbss_addrs[i].addr;
+
+			ether_addr_copy(a, fac);
+			a[0] |= 0x02;
+			a[5] = (a[5] & ~(B43_MBSS_MAX - 1)) | i;
+		}
+		SET_IEEE80211_PERM_ADDR(hw, wl->mbss_addrs[0].addr);
+		hw->wiphy->addresses = wl->mbss_addrs;
+		hw->wiphy->n_addresses = B43_MBSS_MAX;
+	} else if (is_valid_ether_addr(sprom->et1mac)) {
 		SET_IEEE80211_PERM_ADDR(hw, sprom->et1mac);
-	else
+	} else {
 		SET_IEEE80211_PERM_ADDR(hw, sprom->il0mac);
+	}
 
 	/* Initialize struct b43_wl */
 	wl->hw = hw;
